From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 75/78] bench: time SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s verification and the
 whole path of its check

VerifySLHDSA128S times the verification on its own. VerifyScriptP2MRSLHDSA128S
times the whole path of a check as a block validates it: VerifyScript on
a P2MR input with the caching checker, whose cache never fills, over 16
spends with keys and messages of their own, signed when the benchmark
starts, one check per epoch so that -output-json holds the distribution
of single checks. Next to VerifyScriptP2MRSchnorr, these are the
measurements behind the validation weight of the opcode:
C >= 1.25 x 50 x p99(SLH-DSA, worst case) / median(Schnorr), with a
SHA-256 that uses no SHA extensions.
